cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this instrument, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "app-riset-pdp: Instrumen Komparasi Performa OpenCV.js vs face-api.js untuk Presensi Digital Mahasiswa"
abstract: >
  Client-side face detection benchmarking instrument built as a single self-contained
  HTML/JavaScript page. Compares two in-browser face detection pipelines — OpenCV.js
  (Haar Cascade + LBP histogram + cosine similarity) and face-api.js (TinyFaceDetector +
  68-point landmarks + 128-D descriptor + euclidean distance) — under a full 36-scenario
  factorial design (3 lighting levels × 4 pose angles × 3 device tiers). Provides identity
  enrollment, manual and automated 36-scenario trial capture, live per-engine latency/FPS-eq/
  memory metrics, aggregate precision/recall/F1-Score reporting, CSV/JSON export of raw and
  summarized logs, and a client-vs-server latency comparison module that can call a companion
  API (api-riset-pdp, deployed on Cloudflare Workers) or simulate a server-side pathway from
  network parameters (RTT, upload/download bandwidth, server processing time). Developed as
  the data-collection instrument supporting the study "Inovasi Media ICT Deteksi Wajah untuk
  Presensi Digital Mahasiswa: Analisis Akurasi dan Performa" (Sismadi, Manan, & Hartini, 2026),
  under the Penelitian Dosen Pemula (PDP) research grant, Universitas IPWIJA, Jakarta.
